  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: 0 sorries, 0 axioms. fermat_two_square proved: (∃ a b : ℕ, a^2+b^2=p) ↔ p=2 ∨ p%4=1. Mod-4 obstruction via ZMod 4 decidability + Nat.Prime.sq_add_sq for backward. Also inert_prime_not_sum_sq connecting Gaussian prime theory to sum-of-squares impossibility.",
    "builtItems": [
      "sq_mod4_cases: squares in ZMod 4 are 0 or 1 (by fin_cases + decide)",
      "sum_sq_ne_three: ∀ a b : ZMod 4, a^2+b^2 ≠ 3 (by decide)",
      "not_sum_sq_of_mod4_eq_three: p.Prime → p%4=3 → ¬ ∃ a b:ℕ, a^2+b^2=p",
      "fermat_two_square: (∃ a b:ℕ, a^2+b^2=p) ↔ p=2 ∨ p%4=1",
      "fermat_two_square_int: integer form via Int.natAbs_sq",
      "inert_prime_not_sum_sq: combines parent inert_prime with not_sum_sq_of_mod4_eq_three",
      "split_prime_sum_sq: Gaussian int of prime norm gives sum-of-squares witness"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Squares in ZMod 4 are 0 or 1 (4 cases by fin_cases + decide); sum of two squares in ZMod 4 can only be 0, 1, 2 — never 3",
      "ZMod.natCast_eq_natCast_iff + unfold Nat.ModEq + omega gives (p : ZMod 4) = 3 cleanly from p % 4 = 3",
      "Nat.Prime.sq_add_sq requires [Fact p.Prime] typeclass instance; use haveI : Fact p.Prime := ⟨hp⟩",
      "congr_arg Nat.cast + push_cast converts a^2+b^2=p (ℕ) to (a:ZMod 4)^2+(b:ZMod 4)^2=(p:ZMod 4)",
      "inert_prime (from parent BezoutIdentityOQ02OQ01OQ02OQ02) + not_sum_sq_of_mod4_eq_three give dual characterization of inert primes"
    ],
